          <caption>
            <p>Average Costs to a Managed Care Organization. This control chart shows the average costs to a managed care organization over time. In December 2016, costs escalated to more than 3 standard deviations from the mean. By using this chart, the managers at this organization could have realized with a 99.7% certainty threshold, in near real-time, that there was particular cause variation, meaning that there was a real anomaly increasing the costs that they needed to fix, and not just a random variation in costs. M Young, MD, CPHQ</p>
